<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Fuji Creek Trail (Fuji Shelter) from Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:292-3: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.611310" lon="-122.127552"><ele>1249.0</ele><name>Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 554578585); confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; book_elev_ft: 4080; quote: Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park ... At 4,080 feet</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.610084" lon="-122.118756"><ele>1270.2</ele><name>East end of the Salt Creek Falls road</name><desc>source: OSM node 2974554869, east end of way 293880411 'Salt Creek Falls' (day-use/campground road); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 294; quote: the marked trail goes east through the campground then into forest up a short, steep rise. Ski 0.5 mile to a road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.611029" lon="-122.116914"><ele>1280.4</ele><name>Campground road at Highway 58</name><desc>source: OSM node where the Salt Creek Falls access road (way 1173210232) meets State Highway 58; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 294; quote: the marked trail goes east through the campground ... Ski 0.5 mile to a road ... turn left when you reach the road ... and cross the highway</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.611090" lon="-122.116155"><ele>1280.9</ele><name>Road 5894 at Highway 58</name><desc>source: OSM node 40102111, Forest Road 5894 x State Highway 58; confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; quote: turn left when you reach the road 0.5 mile from Salt Creek Sno-Park, and cross the highway ... go east a few paces to Road 5894</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.627602" lon="-122.093010"><ele>1648.0</ele><name>Road 5894 below the shelter</name><desc>source: OSM node 2934509967, the Road 5894 node nearest the shelter; confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; quote: The shelter has been carefully located at the top of a clearcut, above the road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.628717" lon="-122.091823"><ele>1686.8</ele><name>Fuji Shelter</name><desc>source: OSM way 1125733088 Fuji Shelter (wilderness_hut); confidence: high; pdf_page: 294; book_elev_ft: 5600; quote: The shelter has been carefully located at the top of a clearcut, above the road</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Fuji Creek Trail (Fuji Shelter) from Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park</name><desc>1. Salt Creek Falls Sno-Park -&gt; East end of the Salt Creek Falls road: osm (medium), 0.49 mi | 2. East end of the Salt Creek Falls road -&gt; Campground road at Highway 58: osm (medium), 0.13 mi | 3. Campground road at Highway 58 -&gt; Road 5894 at Highway 58: osm (high), 0.04 mi | 4. Road 5894 at Highway 58 -&gt; Road 5894 below the shelter: osm (high), 3.13 mi | 5. Road 5894 below the shelter -&gt; Fuji Shelter: straight (medium), 0.10 mi</desc>
